cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Inria Academy — Advanced Signal Processing Tools"
message: "If you use this material in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Philippe
    family-names: Ciuciu
    affiliation: "Inria, NeuroSpin"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID here
repository-code: "https://github.com/philouc/inria_academy"
url: "https://philouc.github.io/inria_academy/"
abstract: >
  Training material for advanced signal processing methods, covering
  Fourier and wavelet foundations, time-frequency representations
  (STFT, WVD/SPWVD), empirical mode decomposition (EMD, EEMD,
  CEEMDAN), the synchrosqueezing wavelet transform (SST), and
  variational mode decomposition in its univariate (VMD) and
  multivariate (MVMD) forms.
keywords:
  - signal processing
  - time-frequency analysis
  - wavelets
  - empirical mode decomposition
  - synchrosqueezing
  - variational mode decomposition
  - teaching material
